            <div xml:id="d740">

                <pb facs="0988" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg874"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.733/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Trueblood</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-23T11:00:00-05:00">April 23, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Your 33, April 15. Department approves of your protest on ground of
                    international comity in so far as Legation’s telegrams are concerned.</p>
                <p>With respect to taxes on consular telegrams mention may be made of Article XXXIII
                    of the Treaty of 1858.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d740-f1"/></p>
                <p>If exemption is granted to diplomatic or other agents of any country under
                    provisions of a treaty or otherwise you should insist upon like treatment under
                    Article XXX of the same treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
